title: "fix(txpool): handle AlreadyImported race in fork-aware submit_and_watch"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    Fixes a race condition in the fork-aware transaction pool where
    `submit_and_watch` can spuriously return `AlreadyImported` (RPC error 1013)
    even though only a single submission was made. This happens when a concurrent
    `maintain()` call imports the transaction from mempool into a newly-built view
    before `submit_and_watch` gets to submit to that view.

    The fix is implemented in the caller submission paths
    (`submit_and_watch_inner`, `submit_at_inner`, `submit_local`) instead of
    inside `ViewStore::submit_and_watch`:

    - `submit_and_watch_inner` now pre-creates the external watcher before mempool
      insertion, so events emitted by a concurrently-created view are not missed.
    - A snapshot of `most_recent_view` is taken before insertion. If view
      submission later returns `AlreadyImported`, the snapshot is compared with
      the current `most_recent_view`. If it changed, the error is treated as the
      maintain-race and converted to success.
    - On non-race failures after watcher pre-creation, the external watcher is
      explicitly removed, and inserted mempool entries are cleaned up as before.
    - `ViewStore::submit_and_watch` now only submits to active views and
      propagates errors; race detection is handled by callers that have the
      necessary timing context.

    This avoids returning spurious RPC 1013 for the race case while preserving
    normal error handling for non-race `AlreadyImported` paths.

crates:
- name: sc-transaction-pool
  bump: major
